      "writtenOn": "2025-12-02T16:56:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Error Handling in `ft98xx_set_mode`:\n\nIn `fingerprint_ft98xx.c`, within the `ft98xx_set_mode` function, the return code from `ft_sensor_set_mode()` is potentially overwritten by the return code from `ft98xx_enable_irq()` or `ft98xx_disable_irq()`. This means an error from the private library\u0027s mode set function could be masked.\n\nSuggestion: Check the return code from `ft_sensor_set_mode()` first and only proceed to enable/disable IRQ if it was successful. Propagate the error otherwise. Example for FINGERPRINT_SENSOR_MODE_DETECT:\n\n```\ncase FINGERPRINT_SENSOR_MODE_DETECT:\n    if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_HAVE_FT98XX_PRIVATE_DRIVER)) {\n        rc \u003d ft_sensor_set_mode(FOCAL_SENSOR_MODE_DETECT);\n        if (rc \u003d\u003d 0) {\n            rc \u003d ft98xx_enable_irq(dev);\n        }\n    } else {\n        rc \u003d -ENOTSUP;\n    }\n    break;\n```\nThis pattern should be applied to all cases in the switch statement.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 52,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 52,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "c2234ffae14e31247bf85b5d42b00c3fa5b408d5",
